 "new_followers_label": "August",
 "readout_head": "August was the campaign's strongest month, and two trade events are why",
 "readout_extra": [
  "<b>Two trade events carried the month.</b> The Coeliac Australia Gluten-Free Expo (Royal Randwick, Sydney, 15-16 August) and the Fine Food Australia announcement (Melbourne, 31 August to 3 September) shaped the content calendar. The four-day expo window of 13-16 August alone delivered <b>767 of the month's 3,016 Instagram reach</b> and half of its new followers.",
  "<b>Instagram follower growth was the best of the campaign:</b> a net <b>+70</b> for the month, 852 to 922, against +41 in July. Twenty of those arrived on 15 August, the expo's opening day.",
  "<b>Engagement rose on real spread, not a single spike.</b> Interactions reached 227 against July's 146, and accounts engaged 148 against 88. Unlike June, no single day distorts the total - August's busiest day contributed 22 interactions.",
  "<b>Facebook also hit a campaign high:</b> 5,143 organic impressions, up 22% on July, with page fans up 12 to 1,468.",
  "<b>LinkedIn softened and needs attention.</b> 198 impressions against July's 236 and June's 697. Only four posts went out, all long-form thought-leadership, and the 9 August post carried 127 of the 198 impressions on its own. The other three drew 71 between them. Posting cadence is the first thing to look at."
 ],
 "methodology_note": "Follower counts are end-of-month figures. Instagram's total (922) is the live snapshot taken on 1 September, which is the closing August figure; the month's net gain of 70 is measured against July's 852. Windsor.ai's daily series records 77 gross new follows for August, the 7-follow difference being unfollows. LinkedIn's 31 August row was missing from the first data pull and retrieved on a retry, so August's LinkedIn impressions are 198, not the 180 an incomplete pull would show."
}